{
  "_comment": [
    "Formation names for units on the map. Hand-edited — nothing generates this file.",
    "",
    "A map label is two lines: the echelon indicator (II, X, ...) drawn by",
    "EchelonInfo.Indicator, and underneath it the name composed from this file. So a",
    "title here is the name of a formation WITHOUT its echelon — Lancers, not 3rd",
    "Armoured Battalion. The pattern field says how the pieces are put together.",
    "",
    "Matching, in this order:",
    "  1. the first group whose unitIds list contains the type id from units.json,",
    "  2. the first group whose branches list contains its branch,",
    "  3. fallbackTitles.",
    "So id groups are the specific case and branch groups are the net underneath",
    "them; a group may carry both lists. Order inside each pass is file order.",
    "",
    "Every name handed out is unique across the units on the map: the generator",
    "walks ordinal x title from a per-unit starting point and takes the first",
    "combination nobody is using. ordinals x titles is the size of a group pool,",
    "so a group with few titles runs out of numbers sooner — 30 x 8 = 240 here.",
    "",
    "See docs/04-UNITS.md."
  ],

  "pattern": "{ordinal} {title}",

  "ordinals": [
    "1st", "2nd", "3rd", "4th", "5th", "6th", "7th", "8th", "9th", "10th",
    "11th", "12th", "13th", "14th", "15th", "16th", "17th", "18th", "19th", "20th",
    "21st", "22nd", "23rd", "24th", "25th", "26th", "27th", "28th", "29th", "30th"
  ],

